==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|fi|gmq-osw|mānadagher}},<ref>{{R:fi:SSA}}</ref><ref>{{R:fi:NSES}}</ref> or from {{der|fi|gml|māndach}};<ref>{{R:fi:SES}}</ref> ultimately from {{der|fi|gmw-pro|*mānini dag}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=Fi-maanantai.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{enum|fi|sunnuntai|tiistai|day of the week|ma}}
{{fi-noun}}

# [[Monday]] {{gloss|day of the week; the first day of the week in Finland and in the ISO 8601 standard}}

====Usage notes====
As with all days of the week in Finnish, the essive case ({{m|fi||maanantaina}}) is usually used when talking about what will happen or happened on a Monday.

